            <div xml:id="d372">

                <pb facs="0471" n="373" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg373"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Commission/560: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Acting Chairman of the American Delegation to the General Disarmament
                        Conference (Gibson)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-11-28T17:00:00-05:00">November 28, 1932—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>39. [For Wilson.] Your telegram
                    No. 50, November 25, 9 p.m. Has the idea of adopting “declaration of
                    non-recognition of and non-cooperation with Manchukuo Government”, as outlined
                    to you by <pb facs="0472" n="374" xml:id="pg374"/>
                    Drummond and reported in your
                    31, November 1, 9 p.m.,<anchor n="35" xml:id="d372-f1"/> been abandoned?</p>
                <p>Do you not think it highly important that such declaration be made at an early
                    moment? I cannot but feel that failure to do this before proceeding with any
                    plans to shift or narrow responsibility for formulating projects for solution
                    would amount to failure to seize a strategic position while the opportunity
                    exists and the psychological moment is present, and that such failure would add
                    to the difficulty of all subsequent efforts.</p>
                <p>While awaiting your reply to this inquiry, I am formulating tentatively a reply
                    to points raised in your telegram under reference.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
